//! Real-media proof for the beta path: an RTMP publish of genuine H.264/AAC
//! (generated by a REAL ffmpeg `testsrc`/`sine`) goes through the real
//! `RtmpListener` -> `Orchestrator` -> `FfmpegSupervisor` (spawning a REAL
//! ffmpeg) -> `HlsSink`, and the test asserts on what a viewer would get:
//!
//! 1. `index.m3u8` appears and lists >= 2 segments (plus `master.m3u8`),
//! 2. the public HLS router serves the playlist and a segment byte-for-byte,
//! 3. `ffprobe` finds H.264 video + AAC audio and a duration consistent with
//!    the published media, and a full `ffmpeg` decode of the playlist is clean,
//! 4. the stream key appears in no log line (positive control: lines examined).
//!
//! Two scenarios: re-encoding (`transcode_enabled`, libx264) and passthrough.
//!
//! Gated behind the `real-media-e2e` cargo feature. With the feature ON the
//! test never skips: missing `SVC_STREAMING_REAL_FFMPEG` / `_FFPROBE` /
//! `_WORKDIR` is a hard failure. `tests/real_media/run.sh` provisions all
//! three (ffmpeg runs in a digest-pinned container; only docker is needed).

#![cfg(all(unix, feature = "real-media-e2e"))]

